  "explanation": "Cell selection and recording-clock binding live in PyMicroglia. Circadian Workbench owns scientific calls, native figure definitions and vector drawing. Missing observations remain missing, unsupported cells retain visible reasons, and exports retain plotted values, native results, run records and replay scripts. Cohort, spatial and experimental-design workflows remain separate because they cannot be interpreted as an independent analysis of one cell trace. The canonical grid defaults to raw total light, a strict centered three-frame mean and robust linear detrending. Trace grids and native grids share layout and input helpers; compatible numeric wavelet views share one spectrum per cell. Legacy calls preserve their defaults. Live controls submit only the selected analysis settings and jobs report computation, drawing and saving progress. Presentation uses completed data, retains original evidence and exports exact displayed layer and series keys. Native maps stack with independent colour scales. Typed preferences persist across reloads, and paired views expose the reference measurement. Verification passed 48 PyMicroglia and 30 Circadian Workbench tests, browser control/plot checks and strict documentation build. This does not establish independent algorithm validation or that app-wide performance budgets are met. Fitted curves evaluate completed FFT-NLLS components, or use the existing fixed-period descriptive cosinor during trace preparation. Rendering does not fit or repeat period tests.",
  "update_note": "Refresh source fingerprints after final fit-help wording and current UI launch; no numerical behavior changed."
}